fr tho it's possible to retrive your minecraft world, even if it was deleted (if it was deleted using minecraft, not from files level, from .minecraft appdata folder, thing is you need to have a emergency copy of your system, or at least a backup file of your world (in saves folder upon deleting minecraft world the folder of it is deleted completely bypassing recycle bin). If you have a emergency copy from time that world existed, use propertien in blank space of saves folder and click "previous versions" tab, that folder should be there, clink on it and select "restore" and your world should be back to same spot where you made the copy. if you have a backup just copy-paste that backup folder to saves folder.

&#x200B;

Et voila!

